<div class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Free Resource</p>
    <h1>Federal filing checklists</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="wrap" style="max-width:900px;padding:0 20px 40px">
  <div style="border-left:3px solid #14181f;background:#f6f7f9;padding:16px 18px;margin:0 0 28px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0">
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.65">Most filings that fail never reach a judge on the merits. They fail on a deadline, a missing copy, an unexhausted remedy, or the wrong court. These checklists cover the mechanics &mdash; what the rules actually require, and in what order.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="posts">
    {%- for c in checklists %}
    <a class="post" href="/checklists/{{ c.slug }}/">
      <span class="kicker">{{ c.label }}</span>
      <h3>{{ c.title }}</h3>
      <p>{{ c.description }}</p>
      <span class="more">Open the checklist &rarr;</span>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <p style="margin:28px 0 0;font-size:16px">Need the form itself? Every official fillable PDF is in the
    <a href="/forms/">federal court forms library</a> &mdash; unmodified, with a link to the issuing authority.
